# Presence, not content, is what matters.
#
# GitHub Pages runs Jekyll over the published tree unless this file exists, and
# Jekyll silently drops every path beginning with an underscore — which is where
# Next.js puts its entire build output (_next/). The failure mode is a site that
# serves its HTML correctly with no CSS and no JavaScript at all.
#
# Asserted in CI against out/ by scripts/check-export.mjs (F0-05).
